      "note": [
        "Data marked with .. includes classified information or missing data.  \r\n  \r\nMethodological changes  \r\n  \r\nPublication 2022-04-28: Due to a change in deflator for NACE 47.61-47.62 (bookshops; specialised stores for newspapers and stationery) volume (fixed price) series have been revised from January 2016 onwards. Calibration of working day and seasonal adjustment models is not yet done, and adjusted series for 47.61-47.62 are not published since sufficient quality cannot be guaranteed.  \r\n  \r\nPublication 2024-10-29: When publishing the reference month September 2024, changes are implemented that aim to increase the quality of the statistics. The changes involve revisions, in most cases small, from April 2018 to August 2024 and affect the content of tables in the Statistical Database, where some aggregates are added and some are no longer disclosed.  \r\n  \r\nRevisions  \r\n  \r\n2023-01-27: In connection with the publication of reference month December 2022, statistics on specialised stores for home furniture; specialised stores for office furniture (47.591-47.592) between January 2020 and November 2022, were revised. The revisions are due to new information reaching SCB and also apply to all aggregates that include these activities.  \r\n  \r\n2023-11-29: In connection with the publication of reference month October 2023, statistics on opticians (47.781) from reference month May 2023 to September 2023, were revised. The revisions are due to new information received by Statistics Sweden and also apply to all aggregates that include this activity.",
        "2024-01-10: When computing statistics for reference month November 2023, problems with constant price calculations were detected. The problem is due to incorrect weights for price indices being used in calculating constant prices. Checks carried out show that the problem goes back to January 2022. Consequently index series in constant prices have been corrected for all periods back to January 2022.",
        "2024-01-29: In connection with the publication of the reference month December 2023, the statistics have been corrected for periods April 2023 to November 2023. This after it was detected that double counting of objects occurs in the periods. The correction affects industries Non-specialised stores with food, beverages or tobacco predominating (47.11), Opticians (47.781) and Stalls and market stands; other retail sale not in stores, stalls or markets (47.8; 47.99) and aggregates where the industries are included.",
        "2024-02-29: When the reference month January 2024 is published, the base year is changed to 2021. This means that the average of the monthly indices in 2021 is 100 (index 2021=100).",
        "2025-01-30: In connection with the publication of the reference month December 2024, the statistics have been corrected for the periods April 2024 to November 2024. This after an error was discovered in the calculation of final statistics for the second and third quarter of 2024 (final statistics for a given month are published one to three months after the first publication for the month depending on the placement within the quarter). The error stems from the model calculation of the turnover of so-called annual filers, i.e. companies that, due to their turnover size, only need to declare VAT annually. The correction affects all industries within the retail trade. Indices in current prices for total retail trade are corrected by a maximum of 0.1 percentage points.",
        "Correction 2025-05-19: In connection with the new publication of the reference month March 2026, the statistics have been corrected for the period March 2026. The correction affects industries Non-specialised stores with food, beverages or tobacco predominating (47.11) and aggregates where the industries are included.",
        "In connection with the publication of reference month July 2026, a major revision was made for June 2026 in industry for petrol stations (NACE 47.3), due to a previously identified technical error in the imputation of non-response data, which has now been corrected."
      ],
